A||N||7||Zorba||Are i-4 radiators and v6 manual interchangeable?||||5||
Z||000000||Zorba||11-21-2000||03:31 PM||||Can you swap a v-6 radiator into an original 4 for better cooling? Manual tranny.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Rodrv6||11-21-2000||04:09 PM||||According to the 22P parts catalog the same radiator was used in all manual transmission Fieros from 1985-1988, whether equipped with a four or a six.  The only other part number given is for the automatic transmission radiator and they are also common to all 85-88 Fieros regardless of engine.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting :)||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||11-21-2000||05:56 PM||||I would assume the auto-tranny radiators are setup for the tranny cooler lines, where the manuals aren't? I've never seen an auto setup, so don't really know, just a guess.||||reg||1
Z||000003||webbee||11-21-2000||06:38 PM||||56, you're right. The auto is set up for cooling lines from the transaxle and the manual isn't. You can use an auto radiator for both auto and manual.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Archie||11-21-2000||06:58 PM||||Well, I've removed a LOT of stock Fiero radiators. At last count I have 56 4 & 6 cyl. radiators in the loft right now. In all cases the 4 cyl. radiator is about 2/3 the thickness of the 6 cyl. radiator.<P>Archie<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||mrfiero||11-21-2000||07:03 PM||||The 4 cyl. radiators are single row and the V-6 are double row.....that accounts for the thickness difference.<P>I see no problems putting a V-6 radiator in a 4-cyl., but I would be hesitant to put a 4-cyl. one in a V-6.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||007DOUG||11-22-2000||12:42 AM||||I drove all last winter with a 4 banger rad in my 86 GT. <P>Notice I said WINTER. The Gt was my daily beater: at least 150 miles of stop-n-go driving everyday. No overheat problems.||||reg||14
Z||000007||Zorba||11-22-2000||11:12 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Archie:<BR><B>  the 4 cyl. radiator is about 2/3 the thickness of the 6 cyl. radiator.<P>Archie</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>As a temporary measure, isn't a v-6 manual radiator o.k. for a v8 set up while waiting to purchase the 4-core unit you sell? Obviously, if the cooling system has been bled per your instructions, winter and spring should pose no challenges. But I think a 4-core is the way to go. The thickness is double-triple that of a 4 cylinder radiator.<BR>||||reg||1
